# 3D City Simulation — Walkthrough

## What Was Built

A fully interactive **3D city simulation** using Three.js, running entirely in the browser with no backend needed.

![3D City Simulation — Live Screenshot](C:\Users\Menna Gamal\.gemini\antigravity\brain\1da9e737-b5cf-4143-8572-bc536fad9d0f\final_city_simulation_1772757344872.png)

## Project Structure

```
d:\University\3rd year\AI1\3d\
├── index.html          ← Entry point + HUD layout
├── style.css           ← Glassmorphism UI, Inter font
└── js/
    ├── config.js       ← Global constants (grid, road widths, speeds)
    ├── city.js         ← Procedural city: roads, buildings, markings
    ├── traffic.js      ← Traffic lights with phase cycling
    ├── vehicles.js     ← Car AI: lanes, follow-distance, signal obedience
    ├── ui.js           ← HUD stats and button wiring
    └── main.js         ← Scene bootstrap, renderer, animation loop
```

## Features

| Feature | Details |
|---|---|
| 🏙️ City Grid | 5×5 intersections, 4×4 building blocks |
| 🏢 Buildings | Procedural heights (8–50 m), 6 colour families, lit windows |
| 🛣️ Roads | Asphalt surface, white/yellow lane dashes, stop lines, crosswalk stripes |
| 🚦 Traffic Lights | 4 per intersection, NS/EW phase cycling (18s green → 3s yellow → red) |
| 🚗 Cars | 30 default, 15 colours, lane-aware, stop at red, follow-distance AI |
| 🎮 Controls | Orbit / pan / zoom camera, speed slider (0.25×–3×), add cars, reset |
| 🌙 Day/Night | Sky, fog, and car headlight emissive switch on toggle |

## How to Open

> Just open [index.html](file:///d:/University/3rd%20year/AI1/3d/index.html) in Chrome/Edge (double-click the file, or serve via any local HTTP server).

The simulation runs fully offline after Three.js loads from CDN once.

## What Was Tested

- ✅ **3D scene renders** — buildings, roads, cars, and traffic lights all visible
- ✅ **Cars move** — drive in their lane, stop at red, proceed on green
- ✅ **+ Add Cars** — car count increased from 30 → 35
- ✅ **Orbit controls** — camera drag worked smoothly
- ✅ **No console errors** — clean JS execution
- ✅ **HUD** — stats update in real time (car count, elapsed time)
